WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.553 --> 00:00:17.300
The next day at three o'clock, we were back at the front door.

2
00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.762
Once again there was a rustle of silk as the lady of the house approached.

3
00:00:22.923 --> 00:00:24.744
But this time her frown was deeper.

4
00:00:25.824 --> 00:00:29.226
"York, you must put those horses' heads higher," she ordered.

5
00:00:29.246 --> 00:00:31.788
"They aren't fit to be seen."

6
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:39.085
"I beg your pardon, my lady," York said respectfully, "but these horses are not accustomed to wearing a

7
00:00:39.145 --> 00:00:43.709
checkrein. Your husband thought it would be better to get them used to it slowly.

8
00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.573
But if you prefer, I can tighten them up a little more."

9
00:00:47.593 --> 00:00:50.395
"Do so," she said.

10
00:00:52.557 --> 00:00:54.279
York shortened our checkreins himself.

11
00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.182
He did it only slightly, but even that made a difference.

12
00:00:58.983 --> 00:01:00.304
At first it wasn't too bad.

13
00:01:01.984 --> 00:01:06.687
Then we came to a steep hill, and I began to understand why Ginger hated the checkrein so

14
00:01:06.727 --> 00:01:11.871
much. I wanted to put my head forward to help pull the carriage up the hill, as usual.

15
00:01:13.212 --> 00:01:16.814
But this time I couldn't, and my back and legs felt the strain.

16
00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:22.838
"Now you see what it's like," Ginger said when we were back in our stalls.

17
00:01:23.919 --> 00:01:25.040
"It's still not too bad.

18
00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.202
As long as it doesn't get much worse, I'll be fine.

19
00:01:29.303 --> 00:01:30.584
They treat us well otherwise.

20
00:01:31.192 --> 00:01:33.774
But if they try to make it too tight, look out!

21
00:01:34.514 --> 00:01:35.915
I can't bear it, and I won't!"

22
00:01:38.797 --> 00:01:41.959
Day by day, hole by hole, the reins were shortened.

23
00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.582
My work got more and more difficult and uncomfortable.

24
00:01:47.762 --> 00:01:49.824
I used to look forward to being put in harness.

25
00:01:50.704 --> 00:01:51.585
Now I hated it.

26
00:01:53.466 --> 00:01:54.847
Ginger seemed unhappy too.

27
00:01:55.447 --> 00:01:56.828
But she didn't say much about it.

28
00:01:58.108 --> 00:02:01.029
Several days passed where York didn't shorten the reins any more.

29
00:02:01.269 --> 00:02:02.430
I thought the worst was over.

30
00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:04.831
As it turned out, I was wrong.

31
00:02:07.472 --> 00:02:09.293
One day we pulled up to the house as usual.

32
00:02:09.313 --> 00:02:13.095
"Aren't you going to get those horses' heads up, York?"

33
00:02:13.415 --> 00:02:14.355
the lady complained.

34
00:02:14.375 --> 00:02:18.477
"Raise them right now—they've had plenty of time to adjust!"

35
00:02:19.717 --> 00:02:21.538
York nodded without saying anything.

36
00:02:22.539 --> 00:02:23.579
He came to me first.

37
00:02:24.719 --> 00:02:28.821
Lifting my head up, he fastened the checkrein so tightly that I could hardly move.

38
00:02:30.381 --> 00:02:31.342
Next he went to Ginger.

39
00:02:32.542 --> 00:02:35.863
I could see by the look in her eyes that she knew exactly what was coming.

40
00:02:37.043 --> 00:02:39.504
She started jerking her head up and down against the bit.

41
00:02:40.904 --> 00:02:45.906
Then, as soon as York unbuckled the rein to tighten it, Ginger reared up onto her hind legs.

42
00:02:48.687 --> 00:02:52.508
Her knee hit York in the nose, knocking him back so hard that his hat flew off.

43
00:02:53.836 --> 00:02:56.457
He hopped back up right away and rushed toward her head.

44
00:02:57.698 --> 00:03:00.399
A groom standing nearby also tried to grab her.

45
00:03:00.839 --> 00:03:02.300
Ginger was a match for both of them.

46
00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:06.281
She kept bucking, rearing, and kicking out frantically.

47
00:03:07.362 --> 00:03:12.284
At last she tripped over the harness pole and fell, accidentally kicking one of my hind legs on

48
00:03:12.344 --> 00:03:12.924
her way down.

49
00:03:14.445 --> 00:03:16.366
There's no telling what she would have done next.

50
00:03:17.526 --> 00:03:19.327
But this time York was too quick for her.

51
00:03:19.827 --> 00:03:21.828
He sat on her head to keep her from getting up.

52
00:03:23.076 --> 00:03:28.419
Soon several people were cutting Ginger free from her harness, while a groom quickly unbuckled me from the

53
00:03:28.459 --> 00:03:36.962
carriage. He led me back to my stall, put me inside, and hurried off again.

54
00:03:38.843 --> 00:03:40.984
I was still in my harness with my head tied up.

55
00:03:41.704 --> 00:03:44.005
After what had just happened, I was feeling upset.

56
00:03:45.686 --> 00:03:49.408
If I'd ever been the type to kick or rear, I'm sure I would have done it then.

57
00:03:50.924 --> 00:03:56.127
But instead I just stood there, angry and uncomfortable, with my leg throbbing from that kick.

58
00:03:58.088 --> 00:04:00.370
A few minutes later two grooms led Ginger in.

59
00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:02.551
She looked tired and bruised.

60
00:04:04.052 --> 00:04:08.474
York followed, and after watching them put her in her stall, he came to me.

61
00:04:08.494 --> 00:04:13.517
"Stupid checkreins," he muttered as he set my head free.

62
00:04:13.537 --> 00:04:17.660
"I suspected there would be a problem after what Manly told me.

63
00:04:18.792 --> 00:04:21.733
I wish the earl could have talked some sense into his wife.

64
00:04:22.733 --> 00:04:24.354
There was no reason for this to happen."

65
00:04:26.514 --> 00:04:27.754
He noticed my injured leg.

66
00:04:28.815 --> 00:04:32.376
Calling in a groom, he ordered him to clean it and put some lotion on it.

67
00:04:33.916 --> 00:04:35.837
Ginger was never hitched to the carriage again.

68
00:04:37.237 --> 00:04:42.078
When she'd recovered from the incident, the earl's son said he wanted to try her as his riding

69
00:04:42.118 --> 00:04:48.160
horse. As for me, from then on I was paired with a horse named Max.

70
00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:53.982
He was used to the tight checkrein, and one day I asked him how he stood it.

71
00:04:54.002 --> 00:04:58.623
"I bear it because I must," he replied simply.

72
00:04:58.643 --> 00:05:03.425
"But I'm sure it's shortening my life, and it will shorten yours too."

73
00:05:04.626 --> 00:05:05.806
I suspected he was right.

74
00:05:06.947 --> 00:05:10.568
And that made me feel I had no friends at all among the humans at my new home.
